{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "We will use the existing Spring Framework and its ecosystem (e.g., Spring Security, Spring Boot) as the foundation, aligning with the specification's context.",
    "For U1 (Namespace Isolation): We will leverage ZooKeeper (ZK) for tenant metadata isolation. The design will involve creating a tenant-aware configuration path structure in ZK.",
    "For U2 (Admin Authentication): We will implement a standard Spring Security form-based login mechanism to handle username/password authentication for the Admin server.",
    "For U5 (Random Port Access): A spike will research two approaches: a) Direct xd-shell connection to a ZK node that stores the admin server's dynamically registered port, and b) Using a simple Load Balancer (LB) or reverse proxy as an intermediary. The implementation will follow the simpler, more reliable approach identified in the spike, likely the direct ZK lookup for initial implementation.",
    "For U7 (Audio/Video Streaming): We will implement a Motion-JPEG endpoint based on research. The design will focus on creating a framework-agnostic API for frame ingestion, leaving the actual predictive analytics (like facial detection via OpenCV) as an external integration point due to platform compatibility concerns.",
    "For U8 (Message Rates Config): We will add a boolean property to the application's `servers.yml` configuration file (e.g., `spring.management.metrics.export.prometheus.enable-message-rates`). A configuration properties class will bind this value to control the visibility of rate-related metrics in the cluster view component."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The development team is proficient with the Spring Framework, ZooKeeper, and Kafka, as implied by the specification.",
    "The existing system already has ZooKeeper integrated and a working `xd-shell` client.",
    "A continuous integration (CI) and testing infrastructure is in place to run and fix tests (relevant for U6).",
    "The `servers.yml` file is the primary configuration source for the admin server and is accessible at runtime.",
    "The effort estimates are for a single developer. The 'spike' activities (U5, U7) include time for research, decision documentation, and initial proof-of-concept implementation, not a full production-grade solution if the spike reveals major complexity.",
    "The scope of 'clean-up deprecated functions' (U4) is bounded to the functions explicitly mentioned (e.g., module definition download) and related calls within the Shell and Admin-UI modules. No major architectural refactoring is included.",
    "The audio/video streaming requirement (U7) is for the data ingestion and framing part (Motion-JPEG), not the subsequent analytics algorithm implementation."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Implement Tenant Namespace Isolation",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement the tenant-aware namespace structure in ZooKeeper. Modify configuration and service lookups to prefix paths with a tenant identifier derived from the user's profile. Ensure metadata is correctly scoped.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Implement Admin Server Authentication",
      "activity_description": "Implement Spring Security configuration for the Admin server to support a login page where users enter their username and password. Set up the security filter chain and a basic in-memory or LDAP authentication source for initial development.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Create Maintenance Git Branch",
      "activity_description": "Create a maintenance branch (e.g., `maintenance/1.0.x`) from the current master/development branch. Document the branching strategy and update any CI/CD pipeline configurations to build/test this new branch.",
      "most_likely_effort": 0.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Clean Up Deprecated Functions",
      "activity_description": "Identify and remove deprecated functions, such as the module definition download feature. Refactor calling code in the Shell and Admin-UI modules to use current APIs or remove the functionality if obsolete. Ensure tests are updated accordingly.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Spike & Implement Admin Server Port Discovery",
      "activity_description": "Conduct a spike to evaluate approaches for `xd-shell` to discover the admin server's random port. Implement the chosen solution (likely: admin server registers its random port in a known ZK path on startup; `xd-shell` reads this path to connect).",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Upgrade Kafka Client and Fix Tests",
      "activity_description": "Upgrade the Kafka consumer library to the new 0.9 consumer rewrite as referenced. Run the existing test suite for the Kafka message bus integration. Diagnose and fix any test failures caused by the API changes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U7 - Research & Implement Motion-JPEG Ingestion",
      "activity_description": "Research the Motion-JPEG format and design a Spring-based API/controller for streaming ingest of audio/video frames. Implement a prototype endpoint that can receive MJPEG streams. Document the design and integration points for external analytics libraries.",
      "most_likely_effort": 7
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Add Message Rates Configuration Parameter",
      "activity_description": "Add a new configuration property (e.g., `admin.metrics.show-message-rates`) to the `servers.yml` schema. Implement the logic in the Admin UI's cluster view to conditionally display message rate metrics based on this setting.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 23.5
  }
}
```

